  "mathematical_scope": "For fixed positive normal exponent and nonnegative inputs, even-ULP translations preserve rounding, with two parity transitions. Apply a composed block only if its complete sum remains inside that exponent interval; otherwise use the original ordered additions. Both source implementations are removed despite passing independent sequential-addition bit oracles.",
  "validation": "Standalone oracle covers every normal exponent and boundaries, 100000 arbitrary positive sequences, 100000 score sequences and special-value fallbacks. Initial product prototype passes 290 tests and the cost-selector variant 291; both strict Clippy/docs and six full-output screens pass. Memory producers were prepared but not run.",
  "artifact_note": "The initial component-verdict documentation commit failed only for a link-only line; its corrected contextual line and mandatory fast pre-push pass are preserved. No product or runtime criterion changed.",
